\description{
Asks a question of a label set's cells, as a job, in the Spatial view. Neighborhood enrichment: for each pair of labels, the neighbors between their cells in a graph against the number expected if the labels were dealt to the same cells at random (exactly), as a ratio, with a z-score and two-sided p-value from seeded permutations of the labels (within regions, optionally, keeping each one's composition), Benjamini–Hochberg adjusted. Co-occurrence: at each distance, how much likelier each label's cells are within it (or since the distance before) of another label's than of any cell. Nearest distances: each label's cells' distance to the nearest of each label, its median against the labels dealt at random (z, p), and its distribution with an envelope. Ripley's K and L: of each label and across each pair, in a window (the tissue or a region), with Ripley's isotropic edge correction, against the envelope of the labels dealt at random, with a global test. Regions compared: each region's cells by label per mm² of the tissue within it (a density, Garwood's interval) and per labeled cell (a share, Wilson's), the tissue in none of them a row of its own; each region over it as ratios (exact conditional and Koopman's intervals). Across a region's edge: each label's density in bands of signed distance from the edge (inside negative), each band's own tissue its denominator; the core, the margin and around compared, saying which labels fill the region, stay out or gather at its margin. Niches (cellular neighborhoods): each cell's neighborhood (its nearest labeled cells, or those within a radius) by its labels' shares, the cells grouped by k-means with k-means++ seeding into niches, each with its make-up against the tissue's, its defining labels and leading genes, and the niches from further seeds compared by the adjusted Rand index; the niches are a label set too (fill labels:<their id>:0, or niches). Spatially variable genes (moran, of genes, no labels): each gene's Moran's I over a graph, its variances under normality and randomization, the analytic test and permutations, Benjamini–Hochberg over the genes; the leading genes' local Moran's I (each cell high among high, low among low, or unlike its neighbors). A section's cells are not replicates: these describe this section. Recorded as an analysis artifact; asking again answers it. Answers the pairs, the ratios at each distance, the curves, the regions' table, the bands and readings, the niches, or the genes ranked by Moran's I.
}
